From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 19:22:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] context: ks_vm_stats occupancy probe

A diagnostic companion to ks_clear_residual_stack. The idle-point drain
never fired on the poisoned-context repro because frames were
non-empty, so the stack growth is pinned by live suspended executions,
not residue. Expose (frames, stack) so the engine can log occupancy
over time and find what accumulates. Both probes skip the VM's
permanent dummy frame, so frames == 0 means idle.
---
 src/context/mod.rs | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/context/mod.rs b/src/context/mod.rs
index 1823d4b..144240c 100644
--- a/src/context/mod.rs
+++ b/src/context/mod.rs
@@ -506,6 +506,24 @@ impl Context {
         0
     }

+    /// (call frames excluding the dummy, value-stack slots). frames == 0
+    /// with slots left is leaked residue; frames > 0 is a suspended execution.
+    #[inline]
+    pub fn ks_vm_stats(&self) -> (usize, usize) {
+        (self.vm.frames.len().saturating_sub(1), self.vm.stack.len())
+    }
+
+    /// Names of the frames currently pinning the VM, bottom-up (the
+    /// dummy frame excluded). Identifies which suspended execution never completes.
+    pub fn ks_vm_frame_names(&self) -> Vec<String> {
+        self.vm
+            .frames
+            .iter()
+            .skip(1)
+            .map(|f| f.code_block().name().to_std_string_escaped())
+            .collect()
+    }
+
     /// Runs all the jobs with the provided job executor.
     #[inline]
     pub fn run_jobs(&mut self) -> JsResult<()> {
